From 793dd9112e86acf3ce6a98fa6b2e24a9b17bc2ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Malard <malard@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 15:10:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [VideoPlayer][CDebugRenderer] Build the debug overlay's
 subtitle options with the main overlay's code

Since #29150, ResetSubtitlePosition() records the frame height for every
alignment other than manual, and the subtitle overlay compares against
that. The debug overlay kept its own copy of the position tracking and
still compared against the calibration line, so the two never matched
for the default alignment and it reset the player's subtitle position on
every frame while the debug overlay was shown.

The libass render options now come from one helper that takes the
overlay, a style and the display values, and position tracking is split
from style loading so the debug renderer runs the same tracking with its
own style. The debug overlay also skips position tracking until the
frame size is known, as the main overlay does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 7178e3777ba9893dc2b9b2124649943acdeb63b8)
